  "title": "Iran and UAE Hold First BRICS-Level Talks Since Conflict",
  "summary": "Iran and UAE held their first BRICS-level talks since the war began, with Iranian President Pezeshkian meeting UAE Crown Prince Khaled bin Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan in New Delhi. The meeting took place during a BRICS summit and was significant given the severe tensions since the West Asia conflict.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Iran’s President Masoud Pezeshkian met with UAE Crown Prince Khaled bin Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan at the BRICS summit in New Delhi.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The meeting assumed significance as relations between the two sides came under severe strain after Iran targeted many US bases in the UAE in the last few months.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The two leaders discussed strategic partnerships in defense, AI, space, critical minerals, energy, and connectivity.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
