      "title": "Iranian President Pezeshkian meets Abu Dhabi Crown Prince in Delhi",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/iranian-president-pezeshkian-meets-abu-dhabi-crown-prince-in-delhi-126091200974_1.html",
      "description": "Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian held talks with Abu Dhabi Crown Prince Sheikh Khaled bin Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan in New Delhi on the sidelines of the BRICS summit on Saturday.\nThe meeting assumed significance as relations between the two sides came under severe strain after Iran targeted many US bases in the UAE in the last few months as part of its retaliation to the US attacks on Iranian installations.\n\"Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian met with UAE Crown Prince Khaled bin Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan on the sidelines of the BRICS Summit,\" the Iranian embassy said on social media.\nThe meeting came amid reports about Iran's plans Iran to meet members of the Gulf Cooperation Council (GCC) and Iraq in Oman on September 14 to discuss an agreement on transit through the Strait of Hormuz.\nIt will be the first such meeting since the start of the West Asia conflict.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-12T17:59:11"
    },
    {
      "title": "India, UAE review trade and investment ties, discuss new projects",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/india-uae-review-trade-and-investment-ties-discuss-new-projects-126091200964_1.html",
      "description": "India and the United Arab Emirates (UAE) on Saturday explored ways to shore up trade and investment ties with Prime Minister Narendra Modi and Abu Dhabi Crown Prince Khaled bin Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan reviewing the trajectory of bilateral relations.\nThe two leaders met on the margins of the BRICS summit.\nThe meeting came against the backdrop of sudden spike in tensions amid the West Asia conflict.\n\"Discussed taking our Strategic Partnership forward across defence, AI, space, critical minerals, energy, food security and connectivity,\" Modi said in a social media post.\n\"At a time of uncertainty in West Asia, a strong India-UAE is a symbol of stability, prosperity and peace,\" he added.\nIn the trade domain, the two sides discussed ramping up investments by Emirati entities, including by the new sovereign fund L'Imad.\nThe two leaders acknowledged the role that L'Imad, the UAE's newest sovereign investment fund, can play in deepening the bilateral partnership, the Ministry of Exter",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-12T17:41:09"
    }
